   7    1206670  raven-Ran-Elf-Fem-Cha (Poly-Form-Art-Geno) ascended
                 to demigoddess-hood.                         84  [84]

This was, briefly, the fastest ascension of the tournament (20587 
turns). I didn't expect it to hold that position long-term, especially 
since my last game ended at the hands of Orcus after a mere 11k turns. 
That was, potentially, a 13k turn ascension. (My fastest time has since 
been blitzed by Rast.)

Speed records aside, the notable thing here is the insanely low maximum 
of 84 hit points -- beating my previous best by 9.

Fairly standard opening -- shooting stuff, collecting daggers. A couple 
of bones piles yielded numerous scrolls and potions, as did a potion and 
a scroll shop. Grabbed a bag of holding from Sokoban. After finding 
gauntlets of power I ditched the bow and switched to daggers. Killed the 
Minetown priest, converted the altar and made holy water.

I headed downwards, avoiding the Quest for the time being, since I 
didn't have magic resistance or reflection. Found another altar further 
down, and sacrificed until I got Stormbringer. I had a couple of nasty 
incidents with monsters with wands of lightning. Fortunately I was able 
to escape, and got a shield of reflection from an Aleax.

Further on, I dealt with Medusa and stormed the Castle. There were three 
gray dragons in the backrooms; one dropped scales, so I got GDSM. Took 
the wand of wishing (0:3) and wished for a magic marker and speed boots. 
I then headed back to the Quest. Scorpius was pitifully easy; I stood a 
few squares from the stairs and stuck him full of +7 daggers.

Breezed through Gehennom, with plenty of scrolls for magic mapping. Paid 
off Asmo and Baal, killed Juiblex, Vlad and Orcus with little trouble. 
Rodney put in two extra appearances on the way down to the Sanctum, and 
one on the way up. I wasn't bothered much on the Planes; I used conflict 
on Air, Fire and Water to keep the monsters off my back.

On Astral, Death was behind the left-hand door; I killed him with 
daggers twice before making it inside. I fought my way through the 
priests and Angels; Stormy's life-sucking qualities helped keep my hit 
points up. I was slightly worried when Death wandered towards the 
courtyard entrance, but he stayed outside. I made it into the temple, 
and was relieved to find it was the right one.

Conducts: genoless, polyless, artifact-wishless. Finished with level 15, 
AC:-17, +6 Stormbringer and 15 +7 daggers.

